### Done: ORB-R “gap-aware entry” as a v2 fork

- **New strategy**: `orb-retest-breakout-v2` (registered and selectable)
- **Behavior change**: if scanning resumes after a lockout and the **candle opens beyond the trigger**, we now fill off **open** (w/ slippage) instead of “time-machining” back to the trigger.

Here’s the new entry fill logic:

```530:568:/home/broz/code/rockcap/src/lib/backtest/strategies/orb-retest-breakout-v2.ts
    const longHit = candle.high >= longTrigger;
    const shortHit = candle.low <= shortTrigger;

    if (longHit || shortHit) {
      // Determine actual direction from what was hit
      let direction: "long" | "short";
      if (longHit && shortHit) {
        // Tiebreaker
        const distToLong = Math.abs(candle.open - longTrigger);
        const distToShort = Math.abs(candle.open - shortTrigger);
        direction = distToLong <= distToShort ? "long" : "short";
        log(`  Candle[${i}] BOTH triggers hit! Tiebreaker -> ${direction}`);
      } else {
        direction = longHit ? "long" : "short";
        log(`  Candle[${i}] ${direction.toUpperCase()} trigger hit`);
      }

      const slippage = calculateEntrySlippage(direction);
      const triggerPrice = direction === "long" ? longTrigger : shortTrigger;
      const baseFill = direction === "long"
        ? Math.max(triggerPrice, candle.open)
        : Math.min(triggerPrice, candle.open);

      if (
        (direction === "long" && candle.open > triggerPrice) ||
        (direction === "short" && candle.open < triggerPrice)
      ) {
        log(
          `  Gap Entry: open=${candle.open} beyond trigger=${triggerPrice}. Using baseFill=${baseFill}`
        );
      }

      const entryPrice = direction === "long"
        ? baseFill + slippage
        : baseFill - slippage;

      log(`  Entry: ${entryPrice} at ${candle.time}`);
